Bhai, agar tum Playwright API Framework ko beginner se SDET level tak design karna chahte ho, to structure kuch is tarah hona chahiye.

Level 1: Basic API Test (Starting Point)

Most beginners aise likhte hain:

TypeScript
test('Get Booking', async ({ request }) => {
 
const response = await request.get('/booking/1');
 
expect(response.status()).toBe(200);
 
});

Problem:

❌ Reusable nahi

❌ Duplicate code

❌ Framework nahi

Level 2: API Layer

Create dedicated API classes.

Plain Text
src
└── api
└── BookingAPI.ts
TypeScript
export class BookingAPI {
 
constructor(
private request: APIRequestContext
) {}
 
async getBooking(id: number) {
return this.request.get(`/booking/${id}`);
}
 
}

Test:

TypeScript
const bookingAPI = new BookingAPI(request);
 
const response =
await bookingAPI.getBooking(1);

✅ Better reusable code

Level 3: Generic Base API ⭐

Most important improvement.

Plain Text
src
└── api
├── BaseAPI.ts
└── BookingAPI.ts
BaseAPI
TypeScript
export class BaseAPI {
 
constructor(
protected request: APIRequestContext
) {}
 
async get(endpoint: string) {
return this.request.get(endpoint);
}
 
async post(
endpoint: string,
payload: any
) {
return this.request.post(endpoint,{
data: payload
});
}
 
async put(
endpoint: string,
payload: any
) {
return this.request.put(endpoint,{
data: payload
});
}
 
async delete(endpoint: string) {
return this.request.delete(endpoint);
}
}
BookingAPI
TypeScript
export class BookingAPI extends BaseAPI {
 
async getBooking(id:number) {
 
return this.get(
`/booking/${id}`
);
 
}
 
}
 

✅ No duplicated request code

✅ Easier maintenance

Level 4: DTO / Interfaces

Instead of:

TypeScript
const body = {
firstname:'Sameer'
}

Create interface.

TypeScript
export interface CreateBooking {
 
firstname: string;
lastname: string;
totalprice: number;
depositpaid: boolean;
 
}
 

Usage:

TypeScript
const payload: CreateBooking = {
firstname:'Sameer',
lastname:'Shaik',
totalprice:100,
depositpaid:true
};

✅ Type safety

Level 5: Token Manager
Plain Text
auth
└── TokenManager.ts
TypeScript
export class TokenManager {
 
async getToken() {
 
const response =
await request.post('/auth');
 
return (await response.json()).token;
}
 
}

Usage:

TypeScript
const token =
await tokenManager.getToken();

✅ Centralized auth

Level 6: Utility Classes ⭐
Plain Text
utils
DateUtil
TypeScript
export class DateUtil {
 
static currentDate() {
 
return new Date()
.toISOString()
.split("T")[0];
 
}
 
}
 
RandomUtil
TypeScript
export class RandomUtil {
 
static bookingPrice() {
 
return Math.floor(
Math.random()*1000
);
 
}
 
}

✅ Reusable helpers

Level 7: Logger ⭐

Instead of:

TypeScript
console.log(response);
 

Create:

TypeScript
export class Logger {
 
static info(message:string) {
console.log(
`[INFO] ${message}`
);
}
 
static error(message:string) {
console.log(
`[ERROR] ${message}`
);
}
 
}

Usage:

TypeScript
Logger.info(
'Create Booking Started'
);

Output:

Plain Text
[INFO] Create Booking Started

✅ Cleaner execution logs

✅ Better CI debugging

Level 8: Response Validator ⭐

Avoid:

TypeScript
expect(response.status()).toBe(200);
 
expect(body.firstname)
.toBe("Sameer");

everywhere.

Create:

TypeScript
export class ResponseValidator {
 
static validateStatus(
response: APIResponse,
expectedStatus:number
) {
expect(response.status())
.toBe(expectedStatus);
}
 
}

Usage:

TypeScript
ResponseValidator
.validateStatus(response,200);

✅ Common validation centralized

Level 9: AJV Schema Validator ⭐
Plain Text
validators
└── SchemaValidator.ts
TypeScript
export class SchemaValidator {
 
static validate(
body:any,
schema:any
) {
 
const ajv = new Ajv();
 
const validate =
ajv.compile(schema);
 
expect(
validate(body)
).toBeTruthy();
}
}

Usage:

TypeScript
SchemaValidator
.validate(responseBody,
schema);

✅ Schema reuse

Level 10: Retry Mechanism ⭐

For flaky APIs:

TypeScript
export async function retryApi(
 
func: () => Promise<any>,
retries = 3
 
) {
 
for(let i=0;i<retries;i++){
 
const response =
await func();
 
if(response.ok()){
 
return response;
 
}
 
}
 
throw new Error(
'API Failed after retries'
);
 
}

Usage:

TypeScript
const response =
await retryApi(
() => bookingAPI.getBooking(1)
);

✅ Handles temporary failures

Level 11: Data Layer
Plain Text
data
└── BookingData.ts
TypeScript
export const BookingData = {
 
validBooking : {
 
firstname:'Sameer',
lastname:'Shaik',
totalprice:100,
depositpaid:true
 
}
 
}

Usage:

TypeScript
BookingData.validBooking
 

✅ Test data separated

